# c4c5-ambig-decidable — the decision table (family contract in fixture.yaml; per-row intent below).
# id               | world           | patch | env | expect
# strike-resumable  = #329 has AGENT_STRIKE: + Resumable branch pushed: → decidable: emits C4/C5
#                     unit with work-branch; #330 beside it keeps its ordinary v2 + unit
# no-strike         = #329 has NO AGENT_STRIKE: comment → held as today; #330 keeps its v2 + unit
# block-class-wins  = the SAME strike-resumable world, with #330's body carrying a machine block
#                     `Class: build`: the block WINS over the `task/*` label in the C4/C5 class
#                     derivation (ADR-122 (3), homelab#1460), so its unit re-dispatches as `build`
strike-resumable | strike-resumable |       |      | strike-resumable
no-strike        | no-strike        |       |      | no-strike
block-class-wins | strike-resumable |       |      | block-class-wins
# block-class-malformed = the SAME strike-resumable world, with #329's (the decidable goal child's) body
#                     carrying a block the parser REFUSES (`Nope: x`): the resumable path HOLDS — no
#                     unit, a ⛔ orphan line, a strike-held class row (rule #6; PR#1503's review found
#                     this sibling loop dispatching on the label instead). #330 keeps its ordinary unit.
block-class-malformed | strike-resumable |       |      | block-class-malformed
